# End-to-end EMULATOR test: Duet3 6HC (SAME70Q20B) under Renode in tick
# mode. Boots real firmware, completes identify + clocksync, brings up
# the full config (4 TMC5160s on a shared SPI daisy-chain, 2
# software-PWM heaters, fans, endstops, adc_scaled thermistors on the
# SAME70 AFEC) and round-trips M114/M105. See "Per-printer tests" in
# test/emulator/README.md for the shared conventions.
#
# Ground specific to this board: TMC5160 over a SPI DAISY-CHAIN
# (chain_length 6) on usart1. Renode models no USART-in-SPI-mode
# peripheral, so the renode_hooks TMC SPI chain responder hooks
# spidev_transfer by CPU PC, reads MOSI from the firmware buffer,
# synthesises the chain MISO response with a one-transaction-delay-per-
# slot model, and PC-skips the real transfer. DUMP_TMC reads back chain
# positions 1 (stepper_x) and 4 (extruder), proving the chain read path.
#
# Runs the serial-mode build (same70q20b.dict, host link UART2 on
# PD25/PD26) because the pin map is host-link independent;
# duet3_6hc_usb.test drives the identical config over real USB-CDC.
DICTIONARY same70q20b.dict
CONFIG duet3_6hc.cfg
EMULATOR duet3_6hc.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x30"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ZeroDivisionError"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
